implementationPlan.description:
Contract. Edit docs/MCP_SERVER.md, the `### moe.chat_decision` section ONLY (:2716-2733, ending before `### moe.chat_resync`). Other open rows edit other parts of this file, so touch nothing else.

The architect's exact text is the diff at /mnt/d/moe-scratch/314405bb-plan/MCP_SERVER.md.diff:
- Intro: 'Propose a decision for human approval. Optionally post it to a chat channel as `[Decision Proposed] <content>`, sent under the proposer's id.'
- Parameter comments:
  - channel: 'Optional: channel id, or name in either "general" or "#general" form';
  - workerId: 'Optional: proposing worker, a registered worker or "human" (omitted: recorded as "unknown")'.
- Returns: unchanged.
- An Errors list in the file's existing convention (as at :656). Its lead-in is '**Errors.** Every refusal writes nothing: no decision file, no chat message. JSON-RPC code, then `MoeError.codeName`:', followed by four bullets:
  - `-32003 NOT_ALLOWED`: workerId "system" (the moe.chat_send rule);
  - `-32602 INVALID_INPUT`: workerId is not a registered worker or "human", or channel is not a string;
  - `-32001 NOT_FOUND`: channel matches no channel, or matches a name that more than one channel shares;
  - `-32000`: the posted line would exceed the 10KB chat message limit (`Message content exceeds 10KB limit`, as moe.chat_send refuses it).

Adversarial self-review, once (load adversarial-self-review), on `git diff $(git merge-base HEAD "$MOE_LAND_TARGET")` plus the new file.

(a) Mutation check, in a scratch copy of the step-5 snapshot. Use cp -al for node_modules after `rm -rf node_modules/.vite`. Run only the new file per mutant; each mutant must fail at least one case. Then restore and confirm 10/10 green, quoting each run's Tests line. The architect's dry run killed all 7 mutants:
  - M1: today's chatDecision.ts;
  - M2: today's createDecision;
  - M3: skip the 'system' branch;
  - M4: drop the tryLoadWorkerFromDisk fallback;
  - M5: refuse 'human';
  - M6: pass params.channel instead of the resolved id;
  - M7: drop the registered-worker check.
(b) Nothing is written before a refusal: every throw in chatDecision.ts precedes state.createDecision, and the byte check precedes atomicWriteJson.
(c) The contract holds:
  - the success shape and the decision's 9 keys are unchanged;
  - chatSend.ts, the other chat tools and every other MCP_SERVER.md section are untouched;
  - the over-cap error text is byte-identical to sendMessage's.
(d) Edge cases:
  - workerId '' and channel '' behave as omitted;
  - an explicit 'unknown' is refused;
  - an ambiguous channel name is NOT_FOUND, as in chat_send;
  - two concurrent calls stay safe, because createDecision still runs under state.mutex.
(e) Size: `git diff --numstat` against the merge-base. Expect about +175/-10: the dry run was +49/-10 for runtime and docs, plus about 125 lines of test.

Record the review in complete_step.

